fields.Pregnancy Recommendation Free Text:
№50. Can I be vaccinated against COVID-19 if you are pregnant or breast-feeding?
Conclusions of the National Technical Group of Immunization Experts:

1) vaccination of pregnant women should be postponed until the end of pregnancy;

2) if pregnancy occurs after the first dose of the vaccine, the second dose should be postponed until the end of pregnancy;

3) vaccination of pregnant health workers who are assigned to the priority group for vaccination against COVID-19 can be carried out, taking into account the risk-benefit balance, namely, provided that the benefits of vaccination outweigh the high risk of infection and severe COVID-19 in pregnant women;

4) routine pregnancy testing before vaccination against COVID-19 is not recommended;

5) women who are breastfeeding can be vaccinated without reservation.
